{"availability":"available","full":"thakurabhishek7283/tessera-visual","name":"tessera-visual","description":"Image annotation, whiteboard and MapLibre maps with clustering and a location picker. No API keys.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2022-02-14T18:17:12Z","updated":"2026-10-05T13:04:15Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://thakurabhishek7283.github.io/tessera-visual/","topics":["image-annotation","maplibre","maps","w3c-web-annotations","web-components","whiteboard"],"demo":"https://thakurabhishek7283.github.io/tessera-visual/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.922Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.922Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.922Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T23:32:28.259Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-10T03:21:20.922Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Spatial pieces for any web app: image annotation and a whiteboard, and maps with clustering and location picking, with no API keys required. Part of the Tessera kit family: switch a feature on with configuration, use it in any framework, keep the data in the browser or in your own backend.","Marking up a picture and putting places on a map keep coming back in products (a site plan to annotate, a gear photo to point at, a booking form that needs an address), and each time they arrive with a heavy library, an API key and a pile of framework glue. These kits sit on the small Tessera core instead: sets of shapes are stored through a storage adapter, so the same code runs in one browser (which is how the live demo works, with nothing to host), against the reference server, or against your own backend. A feature you do not enable never loads its code, MapLibre is fetched only when a…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/thakurabhishek7283/tessera-visual/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"85b68f7db15974a1cb5fb2aba70f1fc87